# Prelude No. 15 in G major, Well-Tempered Clavier I, BWV 860
# (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a short, sparkling study in triplet broken chords that
# sweep up and down the keyboard, the hands taking turns: one runs the
# arpeggios while the other marks the beat in octaves or eighths. Light,
# fast and good-humoured; over in under a minute.
#
# Time signature and bars: the Bach-Gesellschaft text is in 24/16;
# this Mutopia edition (after Czerny) writes it as 4/4 with triplet
# sixteenths, 19 bars, no upbeat. The MIDI has the same 19 bars.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 88 (a dotted quarter of 24/16), six notes to the
# beat, about 8.8 a second; 76 beats, about 0:54. Track times
# (MusicBrainz track lists): Angela Hewitt (Hyperion, 1998) 0:55 and
# Rosalyn Tureck 0:55, about 83; Edwin Fischer 0:56 and 0:47 (two
# issues); Friedrich Gulda 0:51, about 89; Sviatoslav Richter 0:48,
# about 95; Glenn Gould 0:42, about 108. 88 is between Hewitt and
# Gulda: brisk, and still clear on the chip, where faster arpeggios
# start to blur into a buzz.
#
# Structure (from the Mutopia score, checked against the MIDI; the keys
# are my reading):
#   1-2    G major: arpeggios in the right hand over the G pedal in
#          octave eighths.
#   3      the hands exchange, cadence on D.
#   4-5    a chromatic figure round D (4), then plain scales in eighths
#          (5): toward E minor.
#   6-10   the same pair of ideas in sequence: an arpeggio bar, then
#          an eighth-note bar, through E minor and A minor (the
#          diminished chords in 6 and 8).
#   11-13  the dominant pedal on D: short triplet figures traded over
#          the bass leaping between its two D's.
#   14-16  arpeggios falling in the left hand, the right hand in
#          eighths, back to G (16).
#   17-18  both hands in falling broken chords, the closing sweep.
#   19     the final G major chord, with a fermata.
#
# Range: the left hand's octaves on G (G2 and G3) lose their lower note
# to the chip's range: G2 is lifted to G3, so the opening pedal sounds
# as repeated G's rather than octaves. Other low notes (F-sharp 2, E2,
# D2) are lifted too.

tempo 88

voice mid 0          # two hands, mostly one line each

dyn 1 mf             # bars 1-5: G major, out to the dominant and E minor
dyn 6 mp             # bars 6-10: the sequence through the minor keys,
                     # a quieter manual
ramp 11-13 f         # bars 11-13: the dominant pedal, building
dyn 14 f             # bars 14-19: the return to G and the closing sweep

rit 1.5 0.65         # from the middle of bar 18 into the final chord
